01:01:48,571 --> 01:01:54,571
Drumline is a 2002 American coming-of-age teen
comedy-drama film directed by Charles Stone III.

12
01:07:25,714 --> 01:07:31,714
The screenplay, which was inspired by the Southwest Dekalb High School Marching Panthers
in Decatur, Georgia, was written by Tina Gordon Chism and Shawn Schepps.

13
01:13:02,857 --> 01:13:08,857
The film follows a young drummer from New York, played by Nick Cannon, who enters the fictional
Atlanta A&T University and bumps heads with the leader of his new school's drum section.

14
01:18:40,000 --> 01:18:46,000
Zoe Saldaña, Leonard Roberts and Orlando Jones co-star.

15
01:24:17,142 --> 01:24:23,142
The film received generally positive reviews from critics, with most of
them praising the musical bands' overall performances.

16
01:29:54,285 --> 01:30:00,285
It was a success at the box office, earning over $56 million in the
U.S., and almost $1.2 million in foreign markets.

17
01:35:31,428 --> 01:35:37,428
A direct sequel Drumline: A New Beat, premiered on VH1 on October 27, 2014.

18
01:41:08,571 --> 01:41:14,571
Cannon reprises his role as Devon, albeit as a supporting
character rather than the protagonist.

19
01:46:45,714 --> 01:46:51,714
The film explores themes of sorority, music rehearsal,
fraternity initiation, television broadcast, push ups.

20
01:52:22,857 --> 01:52:28,857
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
